    "post_type": "forum",
    "topic_id": 89767,
    "poster_id": 11062,
    "post_rendered": "Find all couples of polynomials <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/0/74007be33daea5ff2b11838db48328141ce37d15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(P,Q)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"47\" height=\"18\" > with real coefficients, such that for infinitely many <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/7/8f79058700fd8cb5981ea6852cc4d911c81fdfb5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\in\\mathbb R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"13\" > the condition <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/a/38a7c1324f5ee25c68bd6ba50607ef73a406a2df.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[ \\frac{P(x)}{Q(x)}-\\frac{P(x+1)}{Q(x+1)}=\\frac{1}{x(x+2)}\\]\"  width=\"230\" height=\"42\" ><br>\nHolds.<br>\n<i> Nikolai Nikolov, Oleg Mushkarov</i>",
    "post_canonical": "Find all couples of polynomials $(P,Q)$ with real coefficients, such that for infinitely many $x\\in\\mathbb R$ the condition \\[ \\frac{P(x)}{Q(x)}-\\frac{P(x+1)}{Q(x+1)}=\\frac{1}{x(x+2)}\\]\nHolds.\n[i] Nikolai Nikolov, Oleg Mushkarov[/i]",
