   "post_data": {
    "post_id": 524239,
    "post_type": "forum",
    "topic_id": 89768,
    "poster_id": 11062,
    "post_rendered": "a) Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/7/957adc7c1cc7b4708ad0786fb4d5f95ecfdf8d52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{a_n\\}_{n=1}^\\infty$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"60\" height=\"18\" > is sequence of integers bigger than 1. Proove that if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/e/02e28efa00c4f2c66d1aa381c0cb1f8e0ef8d6e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" > is irrational, then <span class=\"aopscode-error aopscode-latex-error\">$\\ds x_n>\\frac{1}{a_{n+1}}$</span> for infinitely many <span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\"  width=\"10\" height=\"8\" >,</span> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/5/195db3e04ee69d85a0aeaedbb1cf9afa97ff4546.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" > is fractional part of <span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/7/9f75ae3b10a68226675858ba052d73aa7405a125.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_na_{n-1}\\dots a_1x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"108\" height=\"10\" >.</span><br>\n<br>\nb)Find all sequences <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/7/957adc7c1cc7b4708ad0786fb4d5f95ecfdf8d52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{a_n\\}_{n=1}^\\infty$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"60\" height=\"18\" > of positive integers, for which exist infinitely many <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/8/8b86ad41bd9668d89a651e8e905ada7fdbc6463e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\in(0,1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"71\" height=\"18\" > such that <span class=\"aopscode-error aopscode-latex-error\">$\\ds x_n>\\frac{1}{a_{n+1}}$</span> for all <span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\"  width=\"10\" height=\"8\" >.</span><br>\n<br>\n<i>Nikolai Nikolov, Emil Kolev</i>",
    "post_canonical": "a) Let $\\{a_n\\}_{n=1}^\\infty$ is sequence of integers bigger than 1. Proove that if $x>0$ is irrational, then $\\ds x_n>\\frac{1}{a_{n+1}}$ for infinitely many $n$, where $x_n$ is fractional part of $a_na_{n-1}\\dots a_1x$.\n\nb)Find all sequences $\\{a_n\\}_{n=1}^\\infty$ of positive integers, for which exist infinitely many $x\\in(0,1)$ such that $\\ds x_n>\\frac{1}{a_{n+1}}$ for all $n$.\n\n[i]Nikolai Nikolov, Emil Kolev[/i]",
